  <static seed="120" source="Library/272/setStewart12_5/problem_16.pg">
    <statement><p>Compare the the planes below to the plane <m>-2 x- y+ 3 z =
-2</m>.  Match the letter corresponding to the words parallel,
orthogonal, or "neither" which describes the relation of the two
planes.</p>
<p><ol>
<li>
<p><m>-2 x+ 3 z = -3</m></p>
</li>
<li>
<p><m>x - 2 y = -5</m></p>
</li>
<li>
<p><m>-10 x - 5 y+ 15 z = 1</m></p>
</li>
</ol></p>
<p><ol label="A.">
<li>
<p>neither</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>parallel</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>orthogonal</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</statement>
